invariant: INV-16
file: widemul.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: widemul_poly1305_avx2 reads the multiply bit alone, so every
  session with it runs the AVX2 kernel and dies of SIGILL on a CPU
  without AVX2. Every vector passes on a CPU with it, because the kernel
  computes the same accumulator. bin/x86_kernels_test counts the
  kernel's calls under every ch_cfg.cpu value, and the script builds it
  for x86-64, where widemul.h compiles the function.

--- old
    return widemul_native(widemul) && (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX2) != 0;
--- new
    (void)cpu;
    return widemul_native(widemul);
